{
  "scene_id": "scene04_two_lives_of_a_system",
  "video_title": "What Is Machine Learning?",
  "scene_title": "The Two Lives of a System",
  "order": 4,
  "duration_mode": "audio_driven",
  "voice": {
    "language": "en-IN",
    "speaker": "priya",
    "model": "bulbul:v3"
  },
  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "s4_01",
      "text": "A machine learning system has two main phases: training and inference."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_02",
      "text": "Training is when the model learns."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_03",
      "text": "Inference is when the model makes predictions."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_04",
      "text": "During training, we give the model many examples, and we already know the correct answers."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_05",
      "text": "The model makes a prediction, compares it to the true answer, and measures the error."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_06",
      "text": "Then it adjusts itself to do better next time."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_07",
      "text": "This happens again and again."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_08",
      "text": "That is how learning takes place."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_09",
      "text": "Inference is different. Once training is done, the model is fixed."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_10",
      "text": "Now we give it new data it has never seen before, and it produces a prediction."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_11",
      "text": "So training is about building the model. Inference is about using it."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_12",
      "text": "The real goal of training is not memorization. The real goal is generalization."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_13",
      "text": "We want the model to learn the underlying pattern well enough that it still works on new examples."
    }
  ],
